✅ 13. Difference Between notify() and notifyAll()

13.1 Definition
notify()
🔴 notify() is a method of the Object class.
🔴 It wakes one arbitrary thread waiting on that object's monitor.
🔴 The awakened thread moves from WAITING to RUNNABLE.
🔴 It does not immediately start executing.

notifyAll()
🔴 notifyAll() is also a method of the Object class.
🔴 It wakes all threads waiting on that object's monitor.
🔴 Every waiting thread moves from WAITING to RUNNABLE.
🔴 They then compete to reacquire the monitor lock.

13.2 Method Signatures
🔴 public final native void notify();
🔴 public final native void notifyAll();

13.3 Why Do We Need Them?

Suppose five threads are waiting.
🔴 Thread-A
🔴 Thread-B
🔴 Thread-C
🔴 Thread-D
🔴 Thread-E

A resource becomes available.
Now we have two choices.

Option 1
Wake one thread.
notify();

Option 2
Wake everyone.
notifyAll();

